          "description": "`Vec::contains` is a linear scan, so testing membership against the output vector inside the loop makes `unique_ids` quadratic in the number of distinct ids. The removed `HashSet` gave amortised constant-time membership, making the function linear. The module documents batches of 100_000 to 500_000 ids on the hot path, where the difference is between a linear pass and on the order of 10^10 comparisons."
